'.\" -*- nroff -*-
.TH KAFS-V7 8 "2026-07-19" "kafs 0.4.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
kafs-v7 \- dedicated format v7 runtime entrypoint
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kafs-v7
.RB --image
.I image
.B --inspection-mount
.I mountpoint
.BR -o " " ro
.RI [ FUSE\ options ]
.br
.B kafs-v7
.RB --image
.I image
.B --controlled-write-mount
.I mountpoint
.BR -o " " rw,no_writeback_cache,no_trim_on_free,bg_dedup_scan=off,fsync_policy=full
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kafs-v7
is the dedicated format v7 runtime entrypoint.
It validates the format v7 CLI boundary, rejects legacy
.B v6_*
mount-option mode tokens, runs descriptor/checkpoint preflight, and admits an
accepted format v7 image for read-only inspection or explicitly bounded
controlled write.
.PP
Inspection admission requires a selected descriptor/checkpoint pair and empty
journal segments.  A clean nonzero checkpoint and a single surviving valid
recovery pair may be mounted read-only.  Divergent or unpaired state fails
closed before FUSE starts.
.PP
The backing image is opened read-only, mapped read-only, and mounted with FUSE
.BR ro .
Mutation requests fail with
.BR EROFS ,
and the selected checkpoint's recovered free-block and free-inode counters are
reported by
.BR statfs (2).
.PP
Controlled-write admission opens the image read-write and requires the explicit
safe option set shown in the synopsis.  It permits only overwrites of existing,
allocated direct blocks in regular files.  A request may span multiple existing
direct blocks while remaining within the current file size.  Partial first and
last blocks use read-modify-COW.  All replacement blocks and inode references
are published in one v7 journal transaction, checkpointed, and then the old
blocks are retired.  Full
.BR fsync (2)
is required for the supported durability contract.
.PP
If a prior controlled write stopped after journal publication, metadata apply,
one checkpoint copy, or partial journal reclaim, the next controlled-write
admission resumes closeout before FUSE starts.  Invalid or incomplete journal
state fails closed.
.PP
Format v6 was an experimental implementation used to split the runtime
entrypoint, descriptor admission, and controlled-write policy away from the
production
.BR kafs (1)
binary.  Format v7 is the breaking-change continuation of that work.  The
current v7 implementation has its own entrypoint, admission, selected runtime
view, layout, and adapter source set and does not route successful admission
through the v6 public wire/layout entrypoint.
.PP
The existing
.B kafs
binary remains the v4/v5 production runtime entrypoint and fails closed for
format v6/v7 images.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.BR --image " " <image>
Specify the format v7 image path.
.TP
.BR --image= "<image>"
Specify the format v7 image path using the inline form.
.TP
.B --inspection-mount
Select the read-only v7 inspection contract.
The request must include
.BR -o " " ro .
.TP
.B --controlled-write-mount
Select the bounded v7 controlled-write contract.  The request must include
.BR rw ,
.BR no_writeback_cache ,
.BR no_trim_on_free ,
.BR bg_dedup_scan=off ,
and
.BR fsync_policy=full .
.TP
.BR --option " " <opt[,opt...]>
Alias for FUSE
.BR -o .
.TP
.BR --option= "<opt[,opt...]>"
Inline form of
.BR --option .
.SH CURRENT LIMITS
File growth, holes, requests beyond the twelve direct blocks, indirect blocks,
file creation, and other metadata mutations are rejected.  Offline repair,
cross-group HRL mutation, and hotplug write delegation are not enabled.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Help was printed.
.TP
.B 2
The request was invalid, the image was not format v7, descriptor preflight
failed, or runtime admission failed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kafs (1),
.BR kafs-v6 (8),
.BR mkfs.kafs (8),
.BR fsck.kafs (8),
.BR kafsdump (8)
.SH AUTHOR
kafs project.
